  "Question": "Simplify \\(\\sin(x-y)\\cos y\\)\\({}+\\cos(x-y)\\sin y.\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\sin x\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\cos x\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\sin x\\cos2y\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\cos x\\cos2y\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The two products have the form of the sine addition formula:\n\\[\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n\\]\nCombining the angles is useful because \\((x-y)+y=x\\). Taking \\(u=x-y\\) and \\(v=y\\), we obtain\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin(x-y)\\cos y+\\cos(x-y)\\sin y\n&=\\sin((x-y)+y)\\\\\n&=\\boxed{\\sin x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThis identity holds for all real angles \\(x\\) and \\(y\\). The answer is choice B.",
